  "notes": [
    "Westend Asset Hub has no GRANDPA of its own (it is parachain 1000, ParachainInfo.ParachainId): B's header is trusted input here. Proving it final through the relay chain (the relay chain's GRANDPA, then this chain's head in the relay chain's state) is out of scope.",
    "Revive.AccountInfoOf(0x2dbe1533a46dda24b00f1a48ef82535e7c1c0bc2) is a contract: trie id 0xf0330cb826a1a7347f09b3a7ee28e1a90844da8f763e0e8a5692f9cf863b87e0, code hash 0x9db319ee6a287a3e631e28768d87d7cc2942f1a86a3f11c6c967cc745fbeb861. Revive.CodeInfoOf of that hash says code_type Evm and code_len 2,106. eth_getCode returns EVM bytecode, which pallet-revive runs with REVM (2,106 B, starting 0x6080604081), and its keccak-256 is that code hash.",
    "state_getChildReadProof served 11 items: the 9 main-trie items that lead to the child root, exactly the items of childRoot.proof, and the 2 child-trie items in slot.proof.",
    "The EVM RPC's block 0x1172df1 is B itself: same hash, parent hash and state root. Revive.BlockHash(B) and Revive.BlockHash(B - 1), proven at B, are 0x1bd8deeea8093a7bf83701596021fdd7bf99e456046cefb9f8fa5404577eb25a and 0x76911163ac19e7c1fe4797fd547eaa237654113a86c6a0643bc71ff3c421763f: the hash and parent hash an eth-rpc that serves the runtime's Ethereum blocks reports for B instead.",
    "eth_getCode and eth_getStorageAt were asked at the EVM block's hash (EIP-1898). eth_getStorageAt returns the proven value byte for byte.",
    "slot.label is the text given with --label; this tool does not check it."
  ]
